 growing 9%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $84K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (3/10).","financial_summary":["Acadia Realty Trust is a mid-cap real estate business with a $3.0B market cap on $411M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +12% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 1% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 8.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 0.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 5.9% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 179% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.7916803391294103},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (21.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Operating margins 11% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 51/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["27 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Acadia Realty Trust (AKR) Could Be 14% Below Fair Value Following Guidance Cut","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/real-estate/nyse-akr/acadia-realty-trust/news/acadia-realty-trust-akr-could-be-14-below-fair-value-followi","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794482890.556,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.922,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"Citigroup Has Lowered Expectations for Acadia Realty Trust (NYSE:AKR) Stock Price","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/09/citigroup-has-lowered-expectations-for-acadia-realty-trust-nyseakr-stock-price.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794250900.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.807,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"(AKR) Movement as an Input in Quant Signal Sets","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/14/AKR_Movement_as_an_Input_in_Quant_Signal_Sets_110826095821_1794193101.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794193101.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"How Investors Are Reacting To Acadia Realty Trust